nd Rebecca Bennett (D) to face off in competitive New Jersey's 7th Congressional District", "source": "Ballotpedia News", "published": "2026-08-13T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 6.11, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": 5.0, "poll_sd": 8.75, "poll_weight": 0.25, "fundamentals": {"margin": 6.2, "lean": 0.0, "environment": 8.2, "incumbency": -2.0, "money": 0.0}, "rating_margin": 6.06, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.83, "baseline_margin": 5.83, "analyst_adjustment": 0.17, "key_factors": ["All nine race ratings favor a Democratic flip, mostly Lean D", "Prediction markets price Bennett's win odds in the mid-80s", "Kean's monthslong absence and disclosed diagnosis have drawn concern even from fellow Republicans", "Kean holds a cash advantage while Bennett benefits from union endorsements and outside-group support"], "rationale": "Race raters unanimously shift the seat toward Democrats, the lone recent poll shows Bennett up five among likely voters, and markets price her near 84%, while Kean's absence from Washington has fueled Republican worry. His fundraising edge and the district's even partisan lean keep this at Lean D rather than stronger.", "watch": "A visible Kean return to the trail or effective SALT-focused attacks on Bennett could tighten the race; fresh polling would clarify.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Thomas Kean Jr. (R) is running."]}, "overview": "New Jersey's 7th District sits at even partisan lean, but every major race rating now favors Democrat Rebecca Bennett to unseat Republican Tom Kean Jr., with most calling it Lean Democratic and several Likely Democratic. The only recent poll, from early September, showed Bennett ahead by five points among likely voters, and prediction markets price her chances in the mid-80s.\n\nKean out-raised Bennett and holds a large cash advantage, but Bennett has picked up union endorsements and outside-group backing while Kean has faced questions after a monthslong absence from Congress and a disclosed depression diagnosis; some New Jersey Republicans publicly worry about his standing. Republicans have attacked Bennett over her position on SALT. The contest remains genuinely competitive, but ratings, polling and markets together point to a modest Democratic edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8072, "margin": 5.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8017, "margin": 5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8142, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8286, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.794, "margin": 6.0}]}